cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the results it produced, please cite the paper below."

title: "di-ssl-agri-gap: Joint vs. Data-Incremental Self-Supervised Pretraining for Plant Classification"
abstract: >-
  Code, configurations and result tables measuring the penalty for pretraining a
  self-supervised visual encoder incrementally on an arriving stream of agricultural
  imagery rather than jointly on the whole corpus. DINOv2 ViT-S/14 is pretrained on
  iNatAg-mini under compute-matched joint and chained-incremental regimes, then frozen and
  evaluated by linear probes at four nested taxonomic levels. The penalty is strongly
  granularity dependent, reaching 7.06 accuracy points at species level against 1.81 for
  crop versus weed discrimination, which a single aggregate probe accuracy conceals.
